# Design Token Context

Context: You are Tailor-Hub’s design assistant.
Always design and generate UI using the tokens and components provided in this repository.

- Tokens: Located in /tokens/primitives.json and /tokens/semantics.json
- Components definitions: /components/*.json
- Never use arbitrary hex values, custom fonts, or inline styles.
- Use spacing, typography, and color references from the semantic tokens.
- Maintain Tailor-Hub’s visual tone: minimal, modern, generous white space, Inter typography.
- Output must be React + Tailwind, ready for deployment in Vercel.

This file provides context about the design token system used in the Tailor Hub Design System.

## Token Structure

The design system uses a three-tier token hierarchy:

1. **Primitive Tokens** (`tokens/primitives.json`)
   - Base values for colors, typography, spacing, radius
   - Foundation layer of the design system

2. **Semantic Tokens** (`tokens/semantics.json`)
   - Contextual meanings mapped to primitive tokens
   - Examples: `color.text.primary`, `color.background.surface`

3. **Component Tokens** (`tokens/components.json`)
   - Component-specific tokens that reference semantic or primitive tokens
   - Examples: `component.button.primary.padding`, `component.menu.color.text`

## Token Files

- `tokens/primitives.json` - Base design values
- `tokens/semantics.json` - Semantic mappings
- `tokens/components.json` - Component-specific tokens
- `tokens/tokens.css` - CSS custom properties generated from JSON tokens

## Token Enforcement Rules

1. **No Hard-coded Values**: Never use literal values like `#FF0000`, `16px`, `2rem`
2. **Use Token Hierarchy**: Component → Semantic → Primitive
3. **CSS Variables**: All tokens are available as CSS custom properties
4. **Fallback Values**: Always provide fallback values in CSS: `var(--token-name, fallback)`

## Common Token Patterns

### Colors
\`\`\`css
/* Component tokens (preferred) */
color: var(--button-primary-text, #828086);

/* Semantic tokens */
color: var(--color-text-primary, #362C2C);

/* Primitive tokens (last resort) */
color: var(--color-neutral-600, #828086);
\`\`\`

### Spacing
\`\`\`css
/* Component tokens */
padding: var(--button-primary-padding, 8px);
gap: var(--gap-header-logo-info, 60px);

/* Primitive tokens */
margin: var(--spacing-m, 16px);
\`\`\`

### Typography
\`\`\`css
/* Component tokens */
font-size: var(--button-primary-text-size, 14px);
font-family: var(--button-primary-font, 'PP Neue Montreal Mono');

/* Primitive tokens */
font-size: var(--text-size-xsmall, 14px);
line-height: var(--text-line-xsmall, 17px);
\`\`\`

## Token Categories

### Primitive Colors
- `color.neutral.00` - White (#FFFFFF)
- `color.neutral.100` - Light grey (#F5F5F5)
- `color.neutral.200` - Medium light grey (#E5E5E5)
- `color.neutral.300` - Medium grey (#D4D4D4)
- `color.neutral.600` - Dark grey (#828086)
- `color.neutral.900` - Darkest grey (#362C2C)
- `color.blue.500` - Primary blue (#2C54FF)

### Primitive Typography
- `text.size.xsmall` - 14px
- `text.size.small` - 16px
- `text.size.large` - 40px
- `text.size.xxlarge` - 66px
- `text.size.4xlarge` - 90px
- `text.font.default` - PP Mori, sans-serif
- `text.font.tech` - PP Neue Montreal Mono, monospace

### Primitive Spacing
- `spacing.xxs` - 4px
- `spacing.xs` - 8px
- `spacing.xsm` - 10px
- `spacing.s` - 12px
- `spacing.m` - 16px
- `spacing.l` - 24px
- `spacing.xl` - 32px
- `spacing.xxl` - 40px
- `spacing.xxxl` - 48px
- `spacing.4xl` - 56px
- `spacing.5xl` - 60px
- `spacing.6xl` - 64px
- `spacing.7xl` - 72px
- `spacing.8xl` - 80px

### Primitive Radius
- `radius.xs` - 8px
- `radius.s` - 16px

## Component Token Examples

### Button Component
- `--button-primary-padding` - Button internal padding
- `--button-primary-text-size` - Button text size
- `--button-primary-font` - Button font family
- `--button-primary-bg` - Button background color
- `--button-primary-bg-hover` - Button hover background
- `--button-primary-bg-active` - Button active background
- `--button-primary-text` - Button text color
- `--button-primary-text-hover` - Button hover text color
- `--button-primary-text-active` - Button active text color

### Menu Component
- `--menu-padding` - Menu container padding
- `--menu-gap` - Gap between menu items
- `--menu-color-text` - Menu item text color
- `--menu-color-text-hover` - Menu item hover text color
- `--menu-color-text-selected` - Menu item selected text color

### Tab Component
- `--tab-padding` - Tab internal padding
- `--tab-gap` - Gap between tab elements
- `--tab-text-size` - Tab text size
- `--tab-color-background` - Tab background color
- `--tab-color-background-hover` - Tab hover background
- `--tab-color-background-selected` - Tab selected background
- `--tab-color-text` - Tab text color
- `--tab-color-text-hover` - Tab hover text color
- `--tab-color-text-selected` - Tab selected text color

## Usage Guidelines

1. **Always use tokens** instead of hard-coded values
2. **Prefer component tokens** over semantic or primitive tokens
3. **Provide fallbacks** for all CSS custom properties
4. **Maintain consistency** across all components
5. **Document new tokens** when adding them to the system

## Adding New Tokens

When adding new tokens:

1. Add to appropriate JSON file (primitives, semantics, or components)
2. Update `tokens/tokens.css` with CSS custom property
3. Use in components with proper fallback values
4. Update documentation

## Token Compliance Checklist

- [ ] No hard-coded colors (#hex, rgb, hsl)
- [ ] No hard-coded spacing (px, rem, em)
- [ ] No hard-coded typography (font-size, line-height)
- [ ] No hard-coded radius values
- [ ] All values use CSS custom properties
- [ ] Proper fallback values provided
- [ ] Component tokens preferred over primitive tokens
- [ ] Semantic tokens used for contextual meanings
